    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39624" root="نذر" body-key="n">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَذِيرَةٌ</span></b>  [<i>A votive gift;</i>] <i>that which he gives who
makes a vow.</i> (M, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>A child appointed
by the father</i> (M, K) <i>and mother</i> (M) [<i>by a
vow</i>] <i>to be a minister,</i> or <i>servant to the church,</i>
(M, K,) or <i>to a place appropriated to religious
services,</i> or <i>exercises,</i> or <i>acts of devotion:</i> (T:)
pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَذَائِرُ</span>. (T.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَذِيرٌ</span>, in two places. ＝ 
 
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  And see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نُذْرٌ</span>.

